%% Primary runtime flow — event ingestion and live stream
%% (observed in backend/src/main/java/click/kivvi/{web/CollectController.java,application/tracking,infrastructure},
%%  frontend/src/composables/useEventStream.ts, mercure/Caddyfile)
sequenceDiagram
  participant Tracker as Tracker / test client
  participant Edge as mercure edge (Caddy + Mercure hub)
  participant Api as CollectController / EventIngestionService
  participant PG as Postgres event_dedup
  participant Hub as Mercure hub (same process as Edge)
  participant SPA as Vue SPA (useEventStream.ts)

  SPA->>Edge: GET /pl/events (SPA document, served by SpaDocumentController)
  Edge-->>SPA: HTML shell + built JS/CSS
  SPA->>Edge: GET /api/v1/pl/events (EventsController -> EventsViewService, 30 seeded rows)
  Edge-->>SPA: JSON view-model
  SPA->>Hub: EventSource /.well-known/mercure?topic=/accounts/1/events (withCredentials)
  Hub-->>SPA: open -> data-stream-state=live

  Tracker->>Edge: POST /collect {idempotency_id, type, ...}
  Edge->>Api: reverse_proxy api:8080
  Api->>Api: TrackedEvent.fromPayload (400 on invalid, PL messages)
  Api->>PG: insert-or-conflict event_dedup(idempotency_hash, expires_at)
  alt duplicate (conflict)
    PG-->>Api: conflict
    Api-->>Tracker: 200 {"status":"duplicate"}
  else new
    PG-->>Api: inserted, 24h TTL
    Api->>Hub: publish {"event": {time,type,typeIcon,tone,detail,customerId?,customerName?,siteName?,siteColor?}} with publisher JWT
    Api-->>Tracker: 202 {"status":"accepted"}
    Hub-->>SPA: SSE message (JSON event)
    SPA->>SPA: render EventRow.vue client-side, prepend, cap 80, unless data-paused
  end

  Note over Api,Hub: A failed publish is NOT caught (HttpMercurePublisher) -> propagates as 500,<br/>by design (matches the pre-migration behaviour this stack replaced).
  Note over PG: Hourly cleanup piggybacks on the same scheduler/ShedLock infrastructure<br/>as the heartbeat job (EventDedupCleanupJob).
